From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taiga Ogawa <zectaiga@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 14:05:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: add Realtek RTL960x switch support

Add a DSA switch driver for the Realtek RTL9607C switch core. It registers
the switch with DSA using the RTL960x GMAC as conduit and the rtl_otto
trailer tag protocol, and offloads bridging, STP, VLANs and the unicast
FDB. On TX the conduit converts the rtl_otto trailer into descriptor port
steering; on RX it attaches a per-source-port metadata dst.

Co-developed-by: Michael Zavertkin <misha.zavertkin@mail.ru>
Signed-off-by: Michael Zavertkin <misha.zavertkin@mail.ru>
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Taiga Ogawa <zectaiga@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/Kconfig
@@ -88,6 +88,8 @@ source "drivers/net/dsa/realtek/Kconfig"
 
 source "drivers/net/dsa/rtl83xx/Kconfig"
 
+source "drivers/net/dsa/rtl960x/Kconfig"
+
 config NET_DSA_RZN1_A5PSW
 	tristate "Renesas RZ/N1 A5PSW Ethernet switch support"
 	depends on OF && (ARCH_RZN1 || COMPILE_TEST)
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/Makefile
@@ -24,5 +24,6 @@ obj-y				+= ocelot/
 obj-y				+= qca/
 obj-y				+= realtek/
 obj-y				+= rtl83xx/
+obj-y				+= rtl960x/
 obj-y				+= sja1105/
 obj-y				+= xrs700x/
